# Make Command Coverage

## Artifact-to-Command Map

This table describes the built-in command family at the time these skills were generated. The local `xf list xf-make` output and command help are authoritative.

| Artifact | Built-in command |
|---|---|---|
| Activity summary definition | `xf-make:activity-summary-definition` |
| Admin navigation | `xf-make:admin-navigation` |
| Admin permission | `xf-make:admin-permission` |
| Advertising position | `xf-make:advertising-position` |
| API scope | `xf-make:api-scope` |
| BB code | `xf-make:bb-code` |
| BB code media site | `xf-make:bb-code-media-site` |
| Class extension and registration | `xf-make:extension` |
| CLI command | `xf-make:cli-command` (`xf-make:command` alias) |
| Code event | `xf-make:code-event` |
| Code event listener | `xf-make:listener` |
| Content-type field | `xf-make:content-type-field` |
| Controller | `xf-make:controller` |
| Cron entry | `xf-make:cron` |
| Entity, optionally finder/repository | `xf-make:entity` |
| Finder | `xf-make:finder` |
| Help page, phrases, and template | `xf-make:help-page` |
| Job | `xf-make:job` |
| Member statistic | `xf-make:member-stat` |
| Public navigation | `xf-make:navigation` |
| Option | `xf-make:option` |
| Option group | `xf-make:option-group` |
| Permission | `xf-make:permission` |
| Permission interface group | `xf-make:permission-interface-group` |
| Phrase | `xf-make:phrase` |
| Repository | `xf-make:repository` |
| Route, optionally related artifacts | `xf-make:route` |
| Service | `xf-make:service` |
| Style property | `xf-make:style-property` |
| Style-property group | `xf-make:style-property-group` |
| Custom make stub publication | `xf-make:stub-publish` |
| Template | `xf-make:template` |
| Template modification | `xf-make:template-modification` |
| Widget definition | `xf-make:widget-definition` |
| Widget position | `xf-make:widget-position` |

Every built-in development-output handler has a corresponding make command. Prefer composed options when creating related artifacts: options can create option groups, permissions can create interface groups, style properties can create style-property groups, listeners can create code events, controllers can create admin permissions or API scopes, and routes can create controllers, templates, navigation, permissions, and API scopes.

Use direct filesystem authoring only when a locally installed add-on introduces a custom development-output handler without a command or UI authoring path. Follow the exceptional fallback documented by `xf-shared-policy` in that case.
